  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 425f70a701d340949ad6110bc3f45d64, type: 3}
  m_Name: SpriteDestructionInfo
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::WorkshopExampleInfo
  m_Scene: {fileID: 102900000, guid: efc672c300f6b1f479882b96c86f2bef, type: 3}
  m_ScenePath: Assets/Examples/SpriteDestruction/SpriteDestruction.unity
  m_ExampleName: Sprite Destruction
  m_Category: Advanced
  m_Purpose: "Demonstrates fragmenting sprites. The physics geometry is broken with the destructor, and each piece gets a sprite cut from the same source texture, so the picture stays consistent across a break.\nClicking a building cuts a hole out of it, and the pieces that come free fall and can be blown apart."
  m_Controls: "Click a building to cut a hole in it.\nFragment Radius: the size of each break.\nCreate Fragments: whether a break leaves debris.\nFragment Count: how many pieces it makes.\nFragment Friction, Fragment Bounciness and Fragment Force: the pieces' friction, bounciness and blast force.\nGravity Scale: how hard gravity pulls.\nThey take effect on the next click."
  m_Description: Demonstrates the use of Sprite fragmenting mapping.
